# Windows batch files MUST be CRLF.
#
# cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only .cmd: it eats a leading character from some lines,
# so `REM CloudFuze …` runs as `CloudFuze …` and `setlocal` runs as `etlocal`, and
# the script fails with "'CloudFuze' is not recognized as an internal or external
# command" instead of doing anything. All three installer scripts shipped that way
# — verified by running the same file twice, LF vs CRLF, on Windows 11.
#
# These are checked out on Linux CI and on macOS too, hence pinning eol rather than
# relying on core.autocrlf, which is a per-clone setting nobody sets.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# The PowerShell helpers are read by powershell.exe, which is tolerant of LF, but
# they sit beside the .cmd files and are edited together — keep them consistent.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
